14. Personal Injury meaning:
Injury,  other  than  bodily  injury,  arising  out  of  one  or  more  of  the following  offences  committed  in  the  course  of  the  Insured's  business, other than its advertising activities:
false arrest, detention or imprisonment;
malicious prosecution;
wrongful entry into, or eviction of a person from a room, dwelling or premises which the person occupies;
invasion of the right of privacy;
oral  or  written  publication  of  material  which  slanders  or  libels  a person  or  organisation,  disparages  a  person's  or  organisation's goods, products or services.

